Two things we are deliberate about. The weights are estimated from the bag type and how full each bag was, and the panel says so, because we do not weigh bags and we are not going to pretend that we do. And general waste is not counted in the impact, because putting waste in a bin is not separating.

### How did you learn about .eco and why did you choose a .eco domain for your site?

I already knew the extension existed before TOTE, and it came back to me when I sat down to register a domain. I looked at what was available, saw .eco in the list, and stopped there.

There were two reasons. The first is that it says what the company is before anyone reads a word. A waste service that needs a paragraph to explain itself has already lost the reader, and tote.eco does that work in the address bar.

The second one matters more to me. Most extensions sell you a name and ask nothing in return. To use a .eco you commit to an environmental purpose and publish it in a profile that anyone can go and read. Ours is at [profiles.eco/tote](https://profiles.eco/tote), and it names the sustainable development goals we work towards. The trustmark sits in the footer of the site.

So it was never decoration. It was the one extension that asked us to say what we stood for, and we were glad to be asked.

